<article class="env-remark" id="09Y2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09Y2">Remark <span data-tag="09Y2">5.28.5</span>.</a> Given a locally finite stratification $X = \coprod X_ i$ of a topological space $X$, we obtain a family of closed subsets $Z_ i = \bigcup _{j \leq i} X_ j$ of $X$ indexed by $I$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  Z_ i \cap Z_ j = \bigcup \nolimits _{k \leq i, j} Z_ k  \]
</div>
  <p> Conversely, given closed subsets $Z_ i \subset X$ indexed by a partially ordered set $I$ such that $X = \bigcup Z_ i$, such that every point has a neighbourhood meeting only finitely many $Z_ i$, and such that the displayed formula holds, then we obtain a locally finite stratification of $X$ by setting $X_ i = Z_ i \setminus \bigcup _{j < i} Z_ j$. </p>
</article>